// 2026-11-21 (landing 177d2e, row 11: DEF-720's row B, form RR6a = RR6s with ARM1; rulings l.22431, l.23411, l.23500, l.23643). A PLACE UNDER THE
// DEREFERENCE OF AN INLINE POINTER EXPRESSION -- a call's result, a ternary, a `??`/`?|` (whose default it may yield), or an unwrap over one -- IS
// ROOTED WHERE THAT EXPRESSION MAY POINT, for a view or an element's address (P3-6's narrowing); before its kind test, an unwrap (`??!`, `?!`) is
// peeled down to a `??`/`?|` and both of that node's sides are collected (ARM1). THE PRICES AT PARITY (l.23411 item 5, l.23500 item 3, l.23643
// ruled item 5, l.23798 item 4), each followed by its twin, refused on main: the self-pointing set's `ap3_rp_c`, `_d` and `_t`; AP3's `ap3_tk_2p`
// and `_2pu`; AFA's eight and ARM1's four with the bare forms and `ap3u_qc_dok`, whose pointer-local twins W2E2 wrote in DEF-732's own `_loc_ok`
// form and measured: each is refused on main, so these are at parity and not DEF-732's off-parity class. The cases have each declared name suffixed
// by the cell's, in the form of main's prices files.
mod:inline_deref_prices;
error:E5;
